[Music]  students at home  keeping connected for halloween with a  virtual choir performance in what's cool  at school  [Music]  late one night when my eyes beheld an  eerie sight a halloween tradition  continues  we always would put together a halloween  performance  and even with 2020 being the year it's  been silvestri junior high school choir  still pulled off their halloween  performance  virtually i wanted to be able to give my  students an opportunity  to where even though they weren't  necessarily singing together in the  classroom  they still were able to experience that  choral  part of being a part of something the  month-long process involved crash  courses on adobe students filming two  separate videos with singing and  choreography  teachers pulling sound files from  sopranos altos  mixing them together to create monster  mash  it was a graveyard smash it was quite a  process to get that it made the hours  and hours of extra time just totally  worth it  for the choir family continuing their  halloween tradition during a pandemic  and the resulting distance learning  they've struggled through  was important maybe even necessary i  wanted them to  to feel like even though covet is going  on that we're still able to maintain  that sense of normalcy we can still  keep those traditions that are important  to to our school and to our choral  family  seems troubled by just one thing all 40  students that took part  lit up when they saw their performance  the best part of the project was  definitely watching their faces when i  showed them the final outcome  [Music]  when you get those videos and you're  watching them and you're like oh  they really are singing behind that  microphone or that bitmoji  figure or whatever it is that they have  on like there really is a kid there  and that's what's cool at school home  edition  if you know something that's cool at  school during these days of distance  learning  let us know about it send us an email  cool at school at 8newsnow.com

